HemoFlow patch to Palabos: index the source block with its own size in
AcceleratedLatticeDataTransfer3D::attribute_static

The envelope copy between two accelerated (GPU) blocks on the same
process indexed the source block's populations with the destination
block's dimensions. The blocks of a sparse decomposition differ in size,
so population i was read from the wrong cell: results off by up to 35 %,
illegal memory accesses or NaN. Only several GPU blocks per process are
affected, not the one-block GPU mode or the CPU.

Added on 22 November 2026 (GPU Phase 5, doc/dev/TODO-GPU.md). Report
upstream and drop this patch once fixed there.

diff --git a/src/atomicBlock/atomicAcceleratedLattice3D.hh b/src/atomicBlock/atomicAcceleratedLattice3D.hh
index 5e937eb..41e405d 100644
